<item name='HelpECategories'><text>1. User Guide</text></item>
<item name='HelpESubCat'><text>Viewing an Order</text></item>
<item name='HelpFCategories'><text>1. Guide d'utilisation</text></item>
<item name='HelpFSubCat'><text>Affichage d'une commande</text></item>
<item name='HelpDocNumber'><number>2</number></item>
<item name='HelpSubCatNumber'><number>2</number></item>
<item name='HelpEHelpText'><richtext>
<pardef id='1' leftmargin='0.8125in' rightmargin='93%'/>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font size='14pt' style='bold' name='Arial' pitch='variable'
 truetype='true' familyid='20' color='blue'/>If you receive a package and do not know who ordered it....</run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font style='bold underline' name='Arial' pitch='variable'
 truetype='true' familyid='20'/>1. If the package has a Packing Slip, you can use any of these means:</run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>	a) Examine the packing slip for the name of the originator</run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>	b) Find the ITA number on the packing slip, then find the owner using the HECS database (see below)</run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>	c) From the packing slip, perhaps you can find the name of the company that the package was purchased from.  Then you can find the owner using the database (see below)</run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font style='bold underline' name='Arial' pitch='variable'
 truetype='true' familyid='20'/>2. If you know which company sent the package</run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>	a) Launch the HECS Orders database by</run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>		1. Launching LotusNotes on your computer</run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>		2. logging into LotusNotes</run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>		3. Launching the HECS Orders database, whose icon looks like this:</run></par>
<par def='1'>		<picture height='93px' width='99px'><gif originalformat='notesbitmap'>
